 diagonal of $B$ will result in switching the corresponding columns in $P.$\n\nFrom our block diagonal matrix\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwe deduce that the first and second columns of $P$ correspond to the complex eigenvector ${v}_{1},$ and the third and forth columns of $P$ correspond to the complex eigenvector ${v}_{3}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 2 & 5 & -5 \\\\ -2 & -7 & -7 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -2 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -5 & -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186388390 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388391 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388390 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388392 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388390 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388393 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388390 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388394 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388390 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388395 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388390 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388390 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388390 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186388394 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388390 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a66467bc-9a50-5d8e-837a-eeefeb49dc48" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388391 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -7 & -7 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 2 & 5 & -5 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -5 & -5 \\\\ -2 & -2 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186388391 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388391 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "81edab10-6956-528b-91cb-f9fb1e627150" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388392 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -7 & 0 & -7 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -7 & 2 & -5 & 5 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -5 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186388392 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388392 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a2a94d76-71ed-5a8e-981f-0131b6dc27f3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] 